\tag{fdip}
\title{Scalar frames and reduced links}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{To compare the [orbit field](fdip-00ZW) at neighboring sites, one
can first rotate each scalar to the same reference value. What then
becomes of the intervening link? The answer depends on how many
group elements carry the reference scalar to a given point.}

\transclude{fdip-010W}
\transclude{fdip-010X}
\transclude{fdip-010Z}
\transclude{fdip-010Y}
\transclude{fdip-0110}
\transclude{fdip-0111}
\transclude{fdip-0112}
\transclude{fdip-0115}
\transclude{fdip-0113}
\transclude{fdip-0114}
\transclude{fdip-0116}
\transclude{fdip-0117}
\transclude{fdip-0118}
